# Touch long-press haptics

When the user **sustains touch** on mobile to trigger an action (context menu, action sheet, drag gate, etc.), provide brief haptic feedback via the **Vibration API**.

Do **not** call `navigator.vibrate` directly in feature code.

## Shared helpers

| Module | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `src/utils/hapticFeedback.ts` | `vibrateLongPressAction()` — call when a custom long-press timer fires |
| `src/utils/initTouchLongPressHaptics.ts` | Bootstrapped in `main.jsx`; covers native `contextmenu` from touch (e.g. sidebar tree) |

Constants: `LONG_PRESS_HAPTIC_MS` (12). Helpers dedupe pulses within ~150ms.

## When to call `vibrateLongPressAction()`

Call it **once**, at the moment the long-press action actually fires (menu opens, sheet opens, drag mode starts, etc.) — not on `pointerdown`.

Typical cases:

- Custom `setTimeout` long-press handlers (`usePressableCardMenu`, chat bubbles, preview table menu, …)
- Touch-only drag gates (e.g. cover editor move after hold threshold)
- Any new coarse-pointer hold gesture that replaces right-click

## Global safety net

`initTouchLongPressHaptics()` listens for touch-derived `contextmenu` and vibrates when no custom handler already did. Custom handlers that call `vibrateLongPressAction()` are deduped automatically.

## Checklist for new touch long-press UI

1. Implement hold with `pointerdown` / `pointermove` slop / `pointerup` (or reuse `usePressableCardMenu`).
2. On action fire → `vibrateLongPressAction()`.
3. On coarse pointers, `preventDefault()` native `contextmenu` when the custom handler owns the gesture.
4. Do **not** add per-feature vibration durations or raw `navigator.vibrate` calls.

```text
❌ BAD — navigator.vibrate?.(12) inline in a component
❌ BAD — long-press menu with no haptic on mobile
❌ BAD — vibrate on pointerdown instead of when the action fires
✅ GOOD — vibrateLongPressAction() when the menu/sheet opens
✅ GOOD — rely on initTouchLongPressHaptics for native contextmenu-only surfaces
✅ GOOD — reuse usePressableCardMenu for card-style long-press menus
✅ GOOD — sidebar tree rows: useTreeRowLongPress + SidebarContextMenu mobileDialog
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
